  "notes": "Spot as a genuine triangle: one defender has both the Flat and the Out and can only take one, so the throw goes to whichever he leaves (force read, bug #76). X's Corner is the last, longest-developing read. Authored from docs/design/intermediate_pass_plays.md; the write-up's Flat->Out->Corner list measured 3.0 air yards against every defense because a mature, wide-open checkdown outranks everything -- the concept is a defender-keyed read, not a progression.",
